    longDescripition:
      '<div class="project-description"><h3>💡 Project Description:</h3><p>This project is a <strong>Movie Website</strong> built as a one-page application to showcase movies currently playing and upcoming releases. The project was first implemented using <strong>HTML</strong> and <strong>CSS</strong>, then later converted to <strong>TailwindCSS</strong> classes during training.  A small amount of <strong>JavaScript</strong> was used to handle the mobile navigation menu.</p><p>The page is structured into multiple sections: a <strong>Hero Section</strong> with a large image, welcoming text, and a booking button; a <strong>Now Showing</strong> section to display movies available this week; a <strong>Coming Soon</strong> section for upcoming films; a <strong>Contact Section</strong> with links and a message input; and a <strong>Footer</strong> with additional information. The design is responsive and adapts well to both desktop and mobile screens.</p><p><strong>Duration:</strong> 1 Day </p><h3>⚙ Technical Features:</h3><ul><li>Responsive header with a collapsible navigation bar for mobile view.</li><li>Hero Section with background image, description, and call-to-action button.</li><li>Movies listing sections: <strong>Now Showing</strong> and <strong>Coming Soon</strong>.</li><li>Contact form with input for sending messages + social links.</li><li>TailwindCSS classes for styling and responsive design.</li><li>JavaScript for toggling the mobile menu.</li></ul><h3>🎯 Challenges & Learning:</h3><p>This project improved my skills in structuring one-page websites, working with <strong>responsive layouts</strong>, and converting a traditional CSS design into <strong>TailwindCSS utility classes</strong>. It also helped me practice integrating <strong>JavaScript</strong> for interactivity, particularly in handling navigation on small screens.</p><p><strong>View Project:</strong> <a href="https://youssef-magdy-19.github.io/Movies_App-master/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Project Link</a></p></div>',
