    desc: "I designed this project by HTML, CSS and JS",
    longDescripition:
      '<div class="project-description"><h3>💡 Project Description:</h3><p>This was my second <strong>JavaScript</strong> project, focusing on building a <strong>Login System</strong> with validation and animations. The login form was implemented with <strong>Regex validation</strong> to ensure that only correct and properly formatted data could be submitted. After a successful login, the user is redirected to a welcome page that dynamically displays a personalized greeting such as “Hi, [username]”, along with a <strong>Logout button</strong> below.</p><p>The project also included smooth animations for the login flow, built using <strong>JavaScript</strong> and <strong>CSS</strong>, creating an engaging experience when typing an email, entering a password, and logging in. The styling was done with <strong>Tailwind CSS</strong> and <strong>HTML</strong>, ensuring a clean and modern responsive design.</p><p><strong>Duration:</strong> 1 Day </p><h3>⚙ Technical Features:</h3><ul><li>Regex-based validation for login inputs (email, password).</li><li>Dynamic greeting that shows the entered username after login.</li><li>Logout functionality with smooth redirection.</li><li>JavaScript + CSS animations for typing and login transitions.</li><li>Tailwind CSS for responsive and modern styling.</li><li>Built using HTML, CSS, Tailwind, and Vanilla JavaScript.</li></ul><h3>🎯 Challenges & Learning:</h3><p>As my second project in <strong>JavaScript</strong>, this helped me dive deeper into form validation, user authentication basics, and adding animations for a better user experience. It was also my first time combining <strong>Tailwind CSS</strong> with JavaScript, which improved both my frontend styling skills and my ability to create interactive, dynamic pages.</p><p><strong>View Project:</strong> <a href="https://youssef-magdy-19.github.io/login-regiseter_pages/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Project Link</a></p></div>',
