    longDescripition:
      '<div class="project-description"><h3>💡 Project Description:</h3><p>A full-stack <strong>Learning Management System (LMS)</strong> built with the MERN stack.The platform serves both <strong>students</strong> and <strong>instructors</strong>, featuring<strong>Clerk</strong> for authentication and <strong>Stripe</strong> for payments. Students can browse,purchase, track progress, and leave ratings; instructors manage courses, monitor students, and review revenue.Significant focus on <strong>frontend ↔ backend integration</strong> with clean REST endpoints, CORS,normalized responses, and robust loading/error states via <strong>Redux</strong> and <strong>Context API</strong>.Implemented <strong>Axios interceptors</strong> and request debouncing where needed.</p><p><strong>Duration:</strong> 2 Weeks </p><h3>⚙ Technical Features:</h3><ul><li><strong>Auth & Payments:</strong> Clerk authentication + Stripe checkout.</li><li><strong>Student:</strong> Course catalog, secure purchasing, progress tracking, ratings.</li><li><strong>Instructor:</strong> Course CRUD, student tracking, revenue overview.</li><li><strong>Stack:</strong> React.js, Node.js, Express.js, MongoDB.</li><li><strong>State/UI:</strong> Redux for app state, Context API for global UI/theme.</li><li><strong>Styling:</strong> TailwindCSS; <strong>Axios</strong> with interceptors; fully responsive.</li><li><strong>API:</strong> Structured REST, consistent JSON, CORS handled, pagination-ready.</li></ul><h3>🎯 Challenges & Learning:</h3><p>Learned to design secure endpoints, stabilize API calls, and keep the UI resilient.Fixed issues around auth headers, checkout edge cases, and optimistic updates.Most importantly: <strong>persistence</strong>—systematic debugging and better logging helped me master<strong>frontend–backend integration</strong> and ship production-style flows with confidence.</p><p><strong>View Project:</strong> <a href="https://edemy-lms-frontend-coral.vercel.app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Project Link</a></p></div>',
